00:41:52.320 --> 00:41:54.680 align:middle line:90%
mentioning, doctors and patients.

00:41:54.680 --> 00:41:58.180 align:middle line:84%
And there'd be one doctor
and multiple patients.

00:41:58.180 --> 00:42:00.950 align:middle line:84%
It would be a turn based game
where you go around and give

00:42:00.950 --> 00:42:01.950 align:middle line:90%
each person a turn.

00:42:01.950 --> 00:42:04.500 align:middle line:84%
The doctor would always be
in relationship to each

00:42:04.500 --> 00:42:06.210 align:middle line:90%
individual one.

00:42:06.210 --> 00:42:11.100 align:middle line:84%
And limited vocabulary I thought
was important, taking

00:42:11.100 --> 00:42:12.660 align:middle line:84%
that from a couple
of the ideas.

00:42:12.660 --> 00:42:14.950 align:middle line:84%
The patient and the doctor each
have their own set of

00:42:14.950 --> 00:42:16.970 align:middle line:84%
vocabularies and the
clash of that would

00:42:16.970 --> 00:42:20.380 align:middle line:90%
introduce mechanic there.

00:42:20.380 --> 00:42:25.375 align:middle line:84%
Where the patient has their own
vocabulary describing to

00:42:25.375 --> 00:42:28.030 align:middle line:84%
the doctor what they like,
what they don't like.

00:42:28.030 --> 00:42:29.240 align:middle line:90%
They know what they like.

00:42:29.240 --> 00:42:37.510 align:middle line:84%
You could extract it to describe
anything the doctor

00:42:37.510 --> 00:42:39.090 align:middle line:84%
would have in their
vocabulary.

00:42:39.090 --> 00:42:43.072 align:middle line:84%
So, as one example the doctor
could give the patient a card

00:42:43.072 --> 00:42:45.530 align:middle line:84%
with a shape or some
item on it.

00:42:45.530 --> 00:42:48.920 align:middle line:84%
And the item has attributes like
color, shape, something

00:42:48.920 --> 00:42:51.190 align:middle line:84%
that somebody could
like or dislike.

00:42:51.190 --> 00:42:56.820 align:middle line:84%
In their list they could look
at this and see one of these

00:42:56.820 --> 00:43:00.450 align:middle line:84%
things clashes with something
in my list of dislikes.

00:43:00.450 --> 00:43:01.460 align:middle line:90%
I don't like that card.

00:43:01.460 --> 00:43:05.760 align:middle line:84%
I'm going to escalate my anger,
my displeasure, with

00:43:05.760 --> 00:43:07.170 align:middle line:90%
the situation.

00:43:07.170 --> 00:43:10.480 align:middle line:84%
And so, the doctor has a limited
amount of time to deal

00:43:10.480 --> 00:43:12.270 align:middle line:90%
with each patient.

00:43:12.270 --> 00:43:16.800 align:middle line:84%
As the patient's escalation
increases, they have less and

00:43:16.800 --> 00:43:18.250 align:middle line:90%
less time to be dealt with.

00:43:18.250 --> 00:43:21.460 align:middle line:84%
After a certain point the doctor
loses that patient, so

00:43:21.460 --> 00:43:24.300 align:middle line:90%
you have that loss brought in.

00:43:24.300 --> 00:43:27.860 align:middle line:84%
And then after all the patients
have been lost the

00:43:27.860 --> 00:43:29.050 align:middle line:90%
game is over.

00:43:29.050 --> 00:43:32.050 align:middle line:84%
The way that it would be won
is that the doctor is

00:43:32.050 --> 00:43:34.180 align:middle line:84%
